<p>Retracting my downvote on the basis of it no longer only feeding on humans. Insects that only target humans are one of my major pet peeves, since I can't imagine any insect evolving that way.</p>
<p>Two new nitpicks, though:</p>
<p>1) There's no such thing as a &quot;Level A hazardous materials suit&quot;. Biohazard safety levels, in order from no containment to &quot;negative-pressurized rooms and full-body suits with external oxygen supply&quot; containment, are Level 0, Level 2, Level 3, and Level 4. You probably meant Level 4.</p>
<p>2) If this thing affects mammals like cats and mice now, and it still only takes 24 hours, you should probably mention something about how a housecat gains 60&#160;kg or so in 24 hours, while comatose, without violating the laws of thermodynamics.</p>

